{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>And shall give light over against its face.</b> That the lamps on the right and the lamps on the left shall be directed toward the central one. And so it is fitting that the intellectual light in the contemplative part, and likewise its light in the practical part, shall face toward the supernal light to serve it with one accord — for then they all give light together, as He testified concerning the menorah, saying (Numbers 8:2–4): בְּהַעֲלֹתְךָ אֶת הַנֵּרֹת אֶל מוּל פְּנֵי הַמְּנוֹרָה וְגוּ' וְזֶה מַעֲשֵׂה הַמְּנוֹרָה מִקְשָׁה — for when all the light is directed toward one, through the מִקְשָׁה (beaten work) which signifies unity, then light is seen radiating from the great luminary."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:18.085392842Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}